  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report 2024's own Segment Reporting note (IFRS 8), 'The Premier Bank PLC.' Total column (Conventional Banking + Islamic banking branches + Off-Shore Banking Unit, i.e. Solo/Bank basis, distinct from the 'Group' column that adds subsidiary Premier Bank Securities Ltd - PBSL); this is the same basis as the report's own 'Performance Highlights for Five Years (2020-2024)' table, confirmed via an exact match on Total Assets (449,626.03) and Profit after Tax (1,454.59, matching the segment note's Bank Total of 1,454,588,947 exactly). IMPORTANT - this is a sector-wide asset-quality shock year for Premier Bank: NPL ratio jumped from 4.99% (FY2023) to 22.92%, classified loans from 14,451.50m to 75,527.14m (5.2x), CRAR fell from 13.58% to 10.54% (below the Bangladesh Bank minimum-plus-buffer requirement of ~12.5%), and Profit before Tax collapsed from 5,260.65m to 1,457.62m on a provision charge of 6,333.76m. Reserve fund: this report's own five-year table states 'Reserve and Surplus' of 17,495.42 for FY2024, but this is arithmetically IMPOSSIBLE against the same table's own Paid-up Capital (12,334.31) and Shareholders' Equity (27,042.86) rows (12,334.31+17,495.42=29,829.73, not 27,042.86); the FY2025 report's comparative column instead shows Reserve and Surplus of 14,708.54 for FY2024, which reconciles exactly (12,334.31+14,708.54=27,042.85~27,042.86) - per project convention, the arithmetically consistent later figure is used here, with this note as the required proof. The Solo entity had a profit (1,454.59m) while the subsidiary PBSL posted a loss (-112.98m), pulling Consolidated/Group PAT down to 1,341.61m - a divergence between Solo and Consolidated performance not seen in prior years. Branches/Employees/Foreign Correspondents sourced from this report's own five-year table.",
